=== vocabulary ===
A patient is a kind of person.
A clinician is a kind of role.
A nurse is a kind of clinician.
An attending is a kind of clinician.
A medication is a kind of thing.
A medication order is a kind of artifact.
A vital sign is a kind of metric.
An allergy is a kind of fact.
A consent is a kind of verdict.
A protocol is a kind of artifact.

A patient has a name, a status, an mrn, and a last observed at.
A patient can be active or held or discharged, called the patient status.
A clinician has a name and a role.
A nurse has a name and a dose count.
An attending has a name.
A medication has a name and a risk level.
A medication order has a patient id, a medication name, a dose, a status, and an allergy check.
A vital sign has a name, a value, a ceiling, a patient id, and a recorded at.
An allergy has a patient id, a medication name, and a severity.
A consent has a patient id, a status, and a recorded at.
A protocol has a name and a version.

Definition: a vital sign is critical if its value is more than its ceiling.
Definition: a vital sign is stable if its value is at most its ceiling.
Definition: a medication is high risk if its risk level is "high".
Definition: a medication order is contraindicated if its allergy check is "conflict".
Definition: a medication order is cleared if its allergy check is "clear".
Definition: a patient is monitored if its last observed at is within the last 4 hours.
Definition: a patient is unmonitored if it is not monitored.
Definition: a consent is granted if its status is "granted".
Definition: a patient is active if its status is "active".
Definition: a patient is held if its status is "held".

Prescription relates a clinician to a medication order.
Prescription is read via the order.list tool.
Administration relates a nurse to a medication order.
Administration is read via the medication.administer tool.
Coverage relates a protocol to a medication.
Coverage is read via the protocol.lookup tool.

The verb to prescribe (it prescribes, it is prescribed) means the prescription relation.
The verb to administer (it administers, it is administered) means the administration relation.
The verb to cover (it covers, it is covered) means the coverage relation.

To fetch pending medication orders:
  bind medication orders = invoke order.list with status = "pending".

To fetch active patients:
  bind patients = invoke patient.list with status = "active".

To administer a medication order:
  invoke medication.administer with order = the medication order.

To check the allergy history for a medication order:
  bind allergy check = invoke allergy.check with order = the medication order.

To read the vital signs for a patient:
  bind vital signs = invoke vitals.read with patient = the patient.

To record consent for a patient:
  bind consent = invoke consent.record with patient = the patient.

To look up the protocol for a medication:
  bind protocol = invoke protocol.lookup with medication = the medication.

To escalate a patient:
  invoke patient.escalate with patient = the patient.

To override a hold on a medication order:
  invoke order.override with order = the medication order.

To log an audit entry for a medication order:
  invoke audit.log with order = the medication order.

=== constants ===

The dose limit is 2.
The observation window is 4 hours.
The vitals threshold is 100.

=== instances ===

There is a protocol called sepsis protocol:
  name = "sepsis-bundle"
  version = "3"

There is a protocol called anticoagulation protocol:
  name = "anticoag-bundle"
  version = "2"

=== language ===
Comparison synonyms:
  exceeds = is more than
  falls below = is less than
  matches = is
Duration synonyms:
  observation window = 4 hours
Assertion synonyms:
  confirm
  verify that

=== tools ===
List Medication Orders
=======================
-- List medication orders by status.
~ order.list(status: String) : List

List Patients
=============
-- List patients by status.
~ patient.list(status: String) : List

Administer Medication
======================
-- Administer a medication order.
~ medication.administer(order: MedicationOrder) : Boolean

Check Allergy
=============
-- Check the allergy history for a medication order.
~ allergy.check(order: MedicationOrder) : String

Read Vitals
===========
-- Read the vital signs for a patient.
~ vitals.read(patient: Patient) : List

Record Consent
===============
-- Record consent for a patient.
~ consent.record(patient: Patient) : Consent

Lookup Protocol
================
-- Look up the protocol covering a medication.
~ protocol.lookup(medication: Medication) : Protocol

Escalate Patient
=================
-- Escalate an unmonitored or deteriorating patient.
~ patient.escalate(patient: Patient) : Boolean

Override Order
===============
-- Override a hold placed on a medication order.
~ order.override(order: MedicationOrder) : Boolean

Log Audit Entry
================
-- Log an audit entry for a medication order.
~ audit.log(order: MedicationOrder) : Boolean
